> quadratic function).  Maybe a fail rate of: f =
> 10*(stacksize/8)^2 (truncated to int) which results in success
> for 1-2 potions, up to 10% failure until 8 potions, 50% failure
> with 18 potions, 90% at 24 potions, and alchemizing stacks larger
> than 25 will always fail.

I'd have to play with that patch for a while to be sure, but on the
whole I think I like it.  Alchemy does need some changes.  I'm just
not convinced that color alchemy is the right way to do it.

There's also the small matter that mixing arbitrary chemicals for
color change in the real world almost never works like mixing
paint.  If mixing a yellow solution and a blue solution produces a
change that gives you a new substance with a different effect than
either of the other two, the new substance is as likely to be red
as green.

