Meh.

I mean, sure, okay, I don't think that would be a problem or
anything, ... but I also can't seem to make myself care about it.

The only times I've seen trolls become a really serious threat have
been when either A) I encounter them earlier in the game than is
normal or B) when I've got bigger problems and the trolls are the
icing on the cake, e.g., I ran across a purple L just above the
castle and he surrounded me with trolls, or I stepped on a magic
trap in the Mines and got blinded and surrounded by six of
something and it turned out they were trolls.  What all of these
cases have in common is, the regeneration isn't really the main
thing that makes the trolls dangerous.

In normal situations, I generally view the fact that trolls
regenerate as a useful, relatively safe source of experience.

The real problem with Trollsbane is that against almost all large
enemies it does only 1d6+1 damage, which is just sad.  A mundane
Elvish short sword, for example, is actually better.


